  "rules": "Cover Identity:\n\nYour character begins each mission with an assigned cover. When performing an action that might expose your cover, roll the Oracle with **Risk**. If the Oracle response is negative or mixed, your cover begins to fray.\n\n* Track cover using **three states**: *Intact*, *Strained*, *Blown*.\n* Each time you act “out of cover,” or draw heat, consult the Oracle and adjust the state.\n* A *Blown* cover immediately triggers **extraction, pursuit, or capture** (Oracle decides which).\n\n> **Tip**\n> Describe how your action fits the cover — not just what you do, but **how you make it look normal**.\n\nInterrogation:\n\nIf captured, you enter an **interrogation sequence**. You must answer questions posed by your captors. For each question:\n\n* You may choose to **Lie**, **Evade**, or **Confess**.\n* Consult the Oracle after each attempt. On a failure, your captors learn something — real or fabricated, Oracle decides.\n* After three questions, roll to see if you’re **released**, **escape**, or remain **detained**.\n\n> **Note**\n> If you plant disinformation during interrogation, note it — it may alter future missions if the lie takes root.\n\nPolitical Tensions:\n\nEach mission alters the geopolitical climate. After a mission:\n\n* Roll the Oracle to determine whether your actions **stabilized**, **disrupted**, or **escalated** tensions.\n* Keep a simple **Tension Track**: *Stable → Shifting → Boiling Point*.\n* At *Boiling Point*, missions become more chaotic: assets disappear, contacts are unreliable, and extraction becomes harder.\n\n> **Tip**\n> Use factions or governments as recurring actors. When you cross one, track their suspicion.",
  "locations": [
    {
      "name": "The Embassy",
      "brief": "An official front for diplomacy, unofficially a nest of surveillance devices, veiled threats, and closed-door deals.",
      "encounters": "Cultural Attaché, Agency Liaison, Surveillance Tech posing as Clerk"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Bazaar",
      "brief": "A volatile maze of whispered deals, cold stares, and vanishing stalls — ideal for covert exchanges and plausible deniability.",
      "encounters": "Information Broker, Disgraced Agent in Hiding, Distraction Team posing as Vendors"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Safehouse",
      "brief": "Nondescript from the outside, the inside tells stories in scratches, gun oil, and half-sanitized medical kits — never truly safe.",
      "encounters": "Paranoid Field Operative, Burned Asset, Silent Quartermaster"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Executive Compound",
      "brief": "A perimeter of decorum hides a core of control — policy is shaped here under velvet threats and soft power.",
      "encounters": "Political Powerbroker, Private Intelligence Consultant, Hidden Microphone"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Grey Sector",
      "brief": "A district of abandoned buildings and flickering streetlamps, known to be both avoided and exploited by operatives of every stripe.",
      "encounters": "Street-Level Informant, Double-Crosser, Surveillance Drone Skimming Rooftops"
    },
    {
      "name": "The Black Lab",
      "brief": "Beyond jurisdiction and ethics, this subterranean site runs tests no one admits exist — the lights hum with secrecy.",
      "encounters": "Nervous Technician, Security AI in Test Mode, Something Not Fully Human"
    }
  ],
  "seeds": [
    "Infiltrate a diplomatic gala and extract a defector hiding in plain sight — before their cover collapses.",
    "A forged memo sparks a scandal. Retrieve the original document before it reaches the press.",
    "Your former handler resurfaces with a job and no explanation. Say yes, or risk losing your identity.",
    "A data vault hidden in a shuttered bookstore may hold the truth behind a blacklisted operation.",
    "Steal a prototype listening device from an ally’s embassy — then decide who gets it.",
    "The safehouse is compromised. Burn the evidence, but someone inside may not be who they claim.",
    "Surveillance footage shows you at a crime scene — but you were never there. Prove it.",
    "A ghost agent transmits from a dead network. Trace the signal before it disappears again.",
    "A staged hostage rescue masks a smuggling op. You're sent in — but to stop which part?",
    "The mole you unmasked has vanished. Your contact insists they were never real.",
    "A message hidden in a vintage broadcast suggests a war-era asset is still active — and watching you.",
    "A poisoned official collapses mid-speech. You have 12 hours to trace the vector before you're blamed.",
    "An encrypted case was dropped in the wrong dead drop. Retrieve it before rival handlers act.",
    "You’re hired to tail a diplomat. They’re already tailing someone else — and so are you.",
    "The target is a child born into a fabricated identity. Extract them, or erase the file.",
    "A former asset demands protection — in exchange for blackmail material you didn’t know existed.",
    "Your cover ID receives an official invitation to a secret summit. You weren’t supposed to be known.",
    "A routine brush pass transfers a drive. It contains footage of your last unsanctioned kill.",
    "Sabotage an arms deal between two factions — but don’t let either know it was you.",
    "A deep-cover operative breaks silence. Their voice sounds like someone you trusted and buried.",
    "A faction wants you to plant intel on a rival. Another pays you to intercept it. Both are watching.",
    "The airport is locked down. One passenger has classified tech in their luggage. Guess who.",
    "You’re offered immunity in exchange for a list of active agents — including your current identity.",
    "A package arrives addressed to your alias. Inside: your real birth certificate and a listening device.",
    "A foreign news outlet publishes details from a mission you haven’t completed yet. Find the leak.",
    "Your mission: escort a scientist across hostile territory. They insist you're part of an experiment.",
    "A key witness is being held in an asylum. They speak only in Cold War ciphers.",
    "A minor bureaucrat is too well-informed. Dig into their past before they dig into yours.",
    "A rogue satellite comes online. It has your old team's encrypted logs — and someone’s using them.",
    "You’ve been framed for an assassination. The evidence is airtight — and planted by your own side.",
    "An encrypted letter arrives weekly, signed by someone who died in a botched mission you led.",
    "An underground courier service moves secrets for hire. Infiltrate it without being archived.",
    "A defector’s memoirs contain details only you should know. Redact the book — or its author.",
    "A facial recognition algorithm tags you in surveillance footage from six years ago — on the wrong side.",
    "A ghost file resurfaces in the archive: classified under your real name. You never wrote it.",
    "Someone is impersonating you across three countries. Trace them — or become them."
  ],
